<h1>Viewers</h1>

<div class="card">
  <p class="muted">
    A <strong>viewer</strong> reads every community in this deployment and changes nothing anywhere.
    Save buttons render disabled for them and the server refuses the write regardless, so the dimension
    is safe to hand out for oversight, a handover, or somebody who needs to see what is going on.
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    Only an administrator grants or revokes it. Viewer spans every community, so an operator of one
    must never be able to hand out oversight of the others. Somebody can hold viewer and operate a
    community at the same time: they read everything, and they change only what an operator of that
    community may change.
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    Somebody who only needs to read <em>one</em> community wants the smaller role instead, under that
    community's Operators section, which an operator there can hand out. This page is the larger ask,
    and it is the only one that cannot be requested by DMing the bot.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Pending requests</h2>
  <% if @viewer_requests.empty? %>
    <p class="muted">No pending viewer requests.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">
      Filed before reading every community stopped being something a DM could ask for. Approving grants
      the row below; denying leaves them exactly where they were and does not block a later ask, which
      is now the community-scoped one.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Requester</th><th>Platform</th><th>Requested</th><th>Decide</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @viewer_requests.each do |req| %>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <%= h(req[:requester_display] || req[:requester_username] || req[:requester_native_id]) %>
              <% unless req[:requester_username].to_s.empty? %>
                <span class="muted">@<%= h(req[:requester_username]) %></span>
              <% end %>
              <div class="muted"><code><%= h(req[:requester_native_id]) %></code></div>
            </td>
            <td><%= h(req[:adapter]) %></td>
            <td class="muted"><%= h(req[:requested_at]) %></td>
            <td>
              <form class="inline" method="post" action="<%= request.script_name %>/viewer-requests/<%= req[:id] %>/approve">
                <button type="submit">Approve</button>
              </form>
              <form class="inline" method="post" action="<%= request.script_name %>/viewer-requests/<%= req[:id] %>/deny">
                <button class="secondary" type="submit">Deny</button>
              </form>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% end %>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Who reads everything</h2>
  <% if @baked_in_viewers.empty? && @granted_viewers.empty? %>
    <p class="muted">Nobody holds viewer status on this deployment.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">
      The rows marked <span class="pill protected">deployment-configured</span> are named in the configuration
      that ships with this deployment. That file is the floor under this table: it can only add
      viewers, and a handle on it keeps reading every community whatever is done here.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Handle</th><th>Platform</th><th>Granted</th><th>By</th><th></th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @baked_in_viewers.each do |entry| %>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <code><%= h(entry[:handle]) %></code>
              <span class="pill protected">deployment-configured</span>
            </td>
            <td><%= baked_in_kind_label(entry[:kind]) %></td>
            <td class="muted">ships with the deployment</td>
            <td class="muted">n/a</td>
            <td class="muted">protected, cannot be removed</td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
        <% @granted_viewers.each do |row| %>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <code><%= h(row[:handle]) %></code>
              <% unless row[:label].to_s.empty? %>
                <div class="muted"><%= h(row[:label]) %></div>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td><%= h(row[:adapter]) %></td>
            <td class="muted"><%= h(row[:granted_at]) %></td>
            <td class="muted"><%= h(row[:granted_by]) %></td>
            <td>
              <form class="inline" method="post" action="<%= request.script_name %>/viewers/<%= row[:id] %>/revoke">
                <button class="danger" type="submit">Revoke</button>
              </form>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% end %>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Grant viewer status</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    Named by the platform handle a person owns, never by their display name, which anyone can set to
    anything. On Matrix that means the full ID (<code>@someone:example.org</code>); everywhere else the
    bare username.
  </p>
  <form method="post" action="<%= request.script_name %>/viewers">
    <p>
      <label>Platform
        <select name="adapter">
          <% @viewer_adapters.each do |adapter| %>
            <option value="<%= h(adapter) %>"><%= h(adapter) %></option>
          <% end %>
        </select>
      </label>
    </p>
    <p><label>Handle <input type="text" name="handle" placeholder="someone" required></label></p>
    <p><label>Name (optional) <input type="text" name="label" placeholder="Ada Lovelace"></label></p>
    <p><button type="submit">Grant</button></p>
  </form>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Hand it over with a token</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    For somebody whose handle you do not have yet. Mint a token, give it to them however you like, and
    they send the bot <code>/auth</code> and the token in a private message. That grants them the role
    and sends them their first sign-in link in the same reply.
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    A token here hands over reading every community, so only an administrator mints one: the token is
    the grant, taken in advance. It works once, it expires whether or not anybody uses it, and it can
    be taken back until it is used. A token for a single community is minted on that community's own
    Operators page instead.
  </p>

  <% if @issued_auth_token %>
    <p><strong>Here is the token. It is shown once and cannot be shown again.</strong></p>
    <p><code><%= h(@issued_auth_token) %></code></p>
    <p class="muted">
      Anybody who has this reads every community on this deployment, so send it over something private
      and do not keep a copy. If it goes astray, revoke it below and mint another.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <h3>Tokens outstanding</h3>
  <% if @auth_tokens.empty? %>
    <p class="muted">No deployment-wide tokens have been minted.</p>
  <% else %>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>For</th><th>State</th><th>Expires</th><th>Minted by</th><th></th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @auth_tokens.each do |row| %>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <% if row[:label].to_s.empty? %>
                <span class="muted">unlabelled</span>
              <% else %>
                <%= h(row[:label]) %>
              <% end %>
              <% unless row[:redeemed_at].nil? %>
                <div class="muted">used by <%= h(row[:redeemed_username] || row[:redeemed_native_id]) %></div>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td><%= h(deps.auth_tokens.state_of(row)) %></td>
            <td class="muted"><%= h(row[:expires_at]) %></td>
            <td class="muted"><%= h(row[:created_by]) %></td>
            <td>
              <% if deps.auth_tokens.live?(row) %>
                <form class="inline" method="post"
                      action="<%= request.script_name %>/auth-tokens/<%= h(row[:public_id]) %>/revoke">
                  <button class="danger" type="submit">Revoke</button>
                </form>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% end %>

  <h3>Mint a token</h3>
  <form method="post" action="<%= request.script_name %>/auth-tokens">
    <p><label>Good for (hours) <input type="number" name="ttl_hours" value="24" min="1" max="336" step="1"></label></p>
    <p><label>Who it is for (optional) <input type="text" name="label" placeholder="Ada, covering the handover"></label></p>
    <p><button type="submit">Mint</button></p>
  </form>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>What has been handed out</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    Every grant, revocation, request and denial, because a role that reads every community everywhere
    is the one worth being able to account for later.
  </p>
  <%= audit_events_table(@viewer_audit, empty: "Nothing recorded yet.") %>
</div>
